{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned","id":506095,"title":"The Unaligned.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-06T14:44:40-07:00","id":506095,"title":"The Unaligned.","content":"I personally enjoy being unaligned. My current game the unaligned are pretty much just dead corpses (hehe) walking who will die of. They're are no unaligned elders or any of kind interaction with them. I'm well aware this is just the story tellers preference and am not complaining but i am just curious how everyone else views and treats them in thier own games. Hopefully we can have a nice long talk about them since not much is really written about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T15:24:40-07:00","id":506131,"title":"","content":"Generally the unaligned become marginalized unless they have some kind of individual edge. If they do have an edge it basically just lets them keep existing without joining one of the big organizations, and they're well advised to stay off the radar. They'll never have any real clout or power, and if they try to tangle with those who do, it won't end well for them.<br /> <br /> Maybe they have good reasons not to get involved in covenant politics, but the price you pay for that autonomy is lack of support.<br /> <br /> ETA: Another way you could run them is by having a large number of unaligned come together to form a sort of local mini-covenant, separate from the big ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T15:32:30-07:00","id":506137,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time fitting them into my game with any significant population unless I want to make a point of a certain character being independent. I like tying NPCs to covenants so they can be involved in the political stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T15:35:30-07:00","id":506139,"title":"","content":"And if the Unaligned gather in numbers around some identity, goal, or methodology that isn't already covered by one of the existing Covenants in a domain ... well, all it takes is a little organization and then you have a new local Covenant.<br /> <br /> So it can be rather hard to make Unaligned characters relevant unless they're player characters, or if there is the rare individual one with a unique position (who is probably a PC, or will be, if one of the PCs is Unaligned).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:26:12-07:00","id":506255,"title":"","content":"As far as I've been able to tell from experience, there are two kinds of unaligned.<br /> <br /> The first is the undecided, who just is biding their time before joining, stalling for various reasons, or hasn't figured out the point yet. They usually join one eventually. Not much to say about them other than they're usually neonates who haven't seen how vicious the world is yet.<br /> <br /> The second kind are the rejects. Either no one wants them, or they're the ones turning their back on the covenants. While the former would be happy to be part of a new organization (if they survive that long), the latter are more keen on going it alone - they often don't want to be part of an organization, the whole reason they went unaligned in the first place! <br /> <br /> Unaligned, of the second kind, are generally lone powers (or a cotorie of lone powers) that set up a little kingdom and have turned their back on the All Night Society. They got their herd, their ghouls, their sires and childer and sisters and brothers, and let the rest of the world burn so long as it doesn't cross their territory's borders.<br /> <br /> There are exceptions, of course, but that's been my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2015, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:53:35-07:00","id":506279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=506139#post506139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the Unaligned gather in numbers around some identity, goal, or methodology that isn't already covered by one of the existing Covenants in a domain ... well, all it takes is a little organization and then you have a new local Covenant.<br /> <br /> So it can be rather hard to make Unaligned characters relevant unless they're player characters, or if there is the rare individual one with a unique position (who is probably a PC, or will be, if one of the PCs is Unaligned).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't help that the covenants are really broad in application. There's an ostensibly unaligned vampire in Immortal Sinners. She's never really met another vampire, or even really met the vampire that sired her, it only appearing as a voice in her head and a pool of Vitae. She's completely unaware of other vampires and believes herself to be a goddess. But through natural inclination and experimentation, she's formed a cult of vampires around herself and discovered Cruac and is effectively a member of the Circle of the Crone, even though she's never heard of it and no one from it has ever spoken to her.<br /> <br /> It's easy to imagine a vampire setting themselves up as a King without knowing about vampire society at large and sort of, over time, developing a system of rulership the Invictus or Carthians might even appreciate.<br /> <br /> Then there's the folks like Zagreus and the Unholy. They're powerful enough and insular enough that they don't really need a covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:58:55-07:00","id":506441,"title":"","content":"I think the Covenants might actually see some benefit in keeping a few unaligned vampires around. Sure they'll be marginalized and mistrusted for the most part, but that could also translate into a certain degree of invisibility. If one covenant can blackmail, threaten, or otherwise cajole one (or more) of the unaligned into acting against their rivals, then they've effectively got a secret weapon that no one is likely to see coming. Better yet, there's little to link them back to the party instigating the attack, particularly if they've concealed their true identity from the unaligned (which would also be an effective means of avoiding betrayal or retribution).<br /> <br /> Of course, pulling something like this would probably only work once or twice (at least with any given unaligned individual), since the target of their attack is likely to flag them as an enemy and pay closer attention from that point on. The unaligned would therefore be pretty much expendable, and things aren't likely to end well for them regardless of how successful they are. Figuring out how to escape this kind of situation could make for a pretty cool scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-07-2015, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:44:34-07:00","id":506712,"title":"","content":"I usually play unaligned as well. I just dont think my play styles or concepts fit into the covenants. I have not had any issues with &quot;being Marginalized&quot; in game. The story teller has always done a great job in finding reasons for me to be .... Useful?<br /> <br /> our group actually played a game where we were all unaligned and sort of banded together to complete a common goal. Like mentioned above. it was great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:34:10-07:00","id":507283,"title":"","content":"It was really good to get other opinions. Overall seems the idea of unaligned is pretty generalized. The Idea of unaligned forming together to form a new covenant or organization is really interesting. I wonder if any examples are in the published books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:50:39-07:00","id":507297,"title":"","content":"<i>Danse Macabre</i> has information on smaller, more specialized covenants. That can be a great place to go for inspiration, or drop-in ready material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:45:05-07:00","id":509133,"title":"","content":"Some bloodlines have their own organizational structure as well, making them technically like mini-covenants unto themselves. One example that comes to mind (since I've spent an inordinate amount of time trying to update them for use in 2nd ed) are the California Xiao from Bloodlines: The Chosen, who are organized as a cult, though one more similar to <i>Heaven's Gate</i> or the <i>Peoples Temple</i> than one of the sects making up the Circle of the Crone. The Kuufukuji are another example, carrying on a communal, monastic existence mostly apart from kindred politics.<br /> <br /> Speaking of monastic sects, the Sakadagami are sort of a mini-Ordo Dracul built around a vampire-focused school of Buddhism, who achieve results similar to the Coils of the Dragon through specialized exercises and intense meditation. As a group, they only really seem to exist in Thailand (and possibly only in Bangkok, at least in any significant numbers), but I could easily see re-imagining the Kuufukuji as a similar sect inspired by the teachings of Thai masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T03:33:29-07:00","id":509766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=506712#post506712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually play unaligned as well. I just dont think my play styles or concepts fit into the covenants. I have not had any issues with &quot;being Marginalized&quot; in game. The story teller has always done a great job in finding reasons for me to be .... Useful?<br /> <br /> our group actually played a game where we were all unaligned and sort of banded together to complete a common goal. Like mentioned above. it was great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not really a defense for Unaligned. As a PC ST is going to make your choice more or less viable. However, if you drop all the PC Aura/Protagonist defenses, unaligned characters will have a much harder time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:44:10-07:00","id":509948,"title":"","content":"Currently in my Vancouver setting, Unbound make up nearly 30% of the recognized kindred. Ordo are the ruling faction (over 30%), and there is a version of the Harbingers and a homebrewed covenant in the mix. There are actually several unaligned as city officers; until recently the Ordo members were secret and assumed to be unaligned as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:11:18-07:00","id":509977,"title":"","content":"I can see perfectly unaligned being tolerated or even promoted by some of the bigs covenants.<br /> <br /> Imagine a domain ruled by very traditionalist Invicti and Sanctified. Carthian and Crone (and may be Dragons) are forbidden.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly possible than the Invicti wouldn't accept all the Kindred in their files. They're elite, they're nobility, Not every kindred is good enough to be part of the Invictus. But also, not everyone is apt for clergyhood (Lancea Sanctum).<br /> <br /> So I think those Invicti and Sanctifies would be happy with most Kindred (the masses) being unaligned, as a third Estate of Kindred. Most unaligned also would be happy of beihg left alone without having to take part in politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:24:29-07:00","id":512439,"title":"","content":"Some people just aren't that much into networking, others may want to socialize but resent authority or overly strict rules and so on - how many people are actively political in day-to-day life?<br /> <br /> Yeah, kindred might have a greater active need of those things than your average human being due to their peculiarities but also suffer greater pressure to resent some aspects of it - so overall i actually treat unaligned as pretty common, invisible, mostly silent when not manipulated but ever present &quot;kindred masses&quot;, undead monsters that interact among each other in a coterie or convenient neighborhoods basis, sometimes surprisingly human in their behaviour due to involving themselves with far more mortals (or the occasional small cliques of other supernaturals) than the than kindred, specially those of the &quot;big parties&quot; in their city.<br /> <br /> How many districts of your own city do you know very well or are very invested in on a daily (or nightly) basis? How many you know because of a job you regularly do or only visit to party (frequently with a group of friends in tow)? How many places are you <b>certain</b> of being able to navigate without any chance of crossing into a bad neighbourhood by mistake or such?<br /> When was the last you thought of it?<br /> <br /> While i certainly amp weirdness and threats considerably (because it's kindred society and the Beast is always there, lurking, for everybody), i mostly interpret the Unaligned through this &quot;faceless masses&quot; lens, their number and proportion varying with the circunstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:32:12-07:00","id":515104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=512439#post512439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people just aren't that much into networking, others may want to socialize but resent authority or overly strict rules and so on - how many people are actively political in day-to-day life?</div> </div> </div> </div> In a number of countries outside of America (renowned for its apathy), the number of people that are card carrying members of a political party is pretty high, actually. So, depending on the location, I'd say, &quot;A lot!&quot; And much higher for vampires, for whom political involvement isn't a want or desire, but very likely is a survival need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T13:54:41-07:00","id":515421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=515104#post515104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a number of countries outside of America (renowned for its apathy), the number of people that are card carrying members of a political party is pretty high, actually. So, depending on the location, I'd say, &quot;A lot!&quot; And much higher for vampires, for whom political involvement isn't a want or desire, but very likely is a survival need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean America as in the country of the USA, or America as in the continent?<br /> Because one of those doesn't apply to me and the culture i took as basis <b>at all</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-15-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T14:46:56-07:00","id":515455,"title":"","content":"I could see a covenant popping up with a focus on capitalism, something similar to bitcoin. Bitecoin? Maybe based around a central Bank of Blood?<br /> <br /> Simple payment for services rendered. Why deal with the intangibles of honor when you can have a straight trade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T20:34:35-07:00","id":515714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=515455#post515455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a covenant popping up with a focus on capitalism, something similar to bitcoin. Bitecoin? Maybe based around a central Bank of Blood?<br /> <br /> Simple payment for services rendered. Why deal with the intangibles of honor when you can have a straight trade?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a sub-faction of the Invictus or even the Carthians? I did have an idea for some kind of social arrangement or Covenant that procures blood dolls or abandoned ghouls to create a large herd that vampires can feed off of for a price. They offer protection and a cut of the money to the discared/abused herds/ghouls of other vampires, and it gives vampires who don't feel comfortable with the risks attached to hunting for their prey another option to feed from a warm, willing vessel without feeling like monsters. IDK, just an idea. I think it would work better as a Carthian experiment, because it's Masquerade-threatening nature wouldn't sit right with the Invictus, although I can see a few in the Invictus participating in this scheme in secret amongst one another or secretly implementing such a scheme to get money and influence among the local unaligned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5746-casper","user":"Casper","date":". 05-15-2015, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5746-casper","name":"Casper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:48:23-07:00","id":516136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=515421#post515421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean America as in the country of the USA, or America as in the continent?<br /> Because one of those doesn't apply to me and the culture i took as basis <b>at all</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> The country. North American and South America are continents - as far as I'm aware, the entire landmass isn't called by that name at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=515455#post515455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a covenant popping up with a focus on capitalism, something similar to bitcoin. Bitecoin? Maybe based around a central Bank of Blood?<br /> <br /> Simple payment for services rendered. Why deal with the intangibles of honor when you can have a straight trade?</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires already trade blood and favors as currency. I imagine they've already got systems in place for it. This is why we have struggles over territory and feeding grounds, after all. Blood is power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T10:06:39-07:00","id":516262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=516136#post516136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires already trade blood and favors as currency. I imagine they've already got systems in place for it. This is why we have struggles over territory and feeding grounds, after all. Blood is power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but like I said, something more regulated and not drowned in the arbitrary intangibility of 'favors'. Flat currency. It would probably be a Carthian offshoot, as Baaldam suggested.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:02:54-07:00","id":516374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=516262#post516262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but like I said, something more regulated and not drowned in the arbitrary intangibility of 'favors'. Flat currency. It would probably be a Carthian offshoot, as Baaldam suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, you are describing the core of the Invictus Oaths. Blood for service is pretty much their most basic Oath of Fealty. Capitalism works with how the different elders of the Estate run things too.<br /> <br /> That said, I doubt it would work. You need trust in a currency for it to function, and vampires don't really need much of anything from other vamps other than blood and favors- what else do they need?<br /> <br /> Even in modern day society, money is nothing more than a promissory note for access to other kinds of needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-16-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T13:33:28-07:00","id":516429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=516262#post516262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but like I said, something more regulated and not drowned in the arbitrary intangibility of 'favors'. Flat currency.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me; was the concept of prestation ever carried over from Masquerade, either as a formal code of conduct or as loose de facto social interaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T13:59:18-07:00","id":516443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=516374#post516374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, you are describing the core of the Invictus Oaths. Blood for service is pretty much their most basic Oath of Fealty. Capitalism works with how the different elders of the Estate run things too.<br /> <br /> That said, I doubt it would work. You need trust in a currency for it to function, and vampires don't really need much of anything from other vamps other than blood and favors- what else do they need?<br /> <br /> Even in modern day society, money is nothing more than a promissory note for access to other kinds of needs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood Money. How was the modern money given value at the start? They were slips of promisary notes, which you could exchange into gold in a bank, thus giving them value. Create a vampire bank, which gives out promisary notes (money) which can be exchanged into blood. As a vampire, you provide blood/blood dolls to the bank, which gives out you this blood money to you, and you can go exchange the money with others knowing that there's value in it. If the bank is run by the vampire government, they can even instantiate taxes (X Blood Moneys / month must be paid for the civil duties) and then you can even have wages to the city officials/hounds/etc, in addition to giving them feeding grounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:01:37-07:00","id":516445,"title":"","content":"That's an intriguing idea. Counterfeit comes to mind. You could have a specialized devotion, or maybe even a bloodline that runs the bank. They mark all official Blood Money notes with a drop of blood that they can recognize later. Sorta like the strips or watermarks in US currency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T15:04:34-07:00","id":516500,"title":"","content":"Counterfeit would be a big problem. And it can't simply be blood. Elders don't need animal, or human blood. It would have to be a special kind of blood, or at least 'lesser' blood would be worth, well, less.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Bankers have created a bloodline of vampires that cannot inflict the Vinculum, allowing access to top level blood. Obviously you have a problem with other bloodlines with the same blessed curse. Maybe they can only Embrace people with the Producer merit, or they have the Honey Trap merit as a bonus to their bloodline. Scattered across the world in cold rooms would be herds of vampires fed on animal or human blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-16-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T15:10:32-07:00","id":516504,"title":"","content":"I always try to avoid having my players or npcs belong to a covenant (Or associated faction for other races) as unaligned or their equivalent are almost always disapproved of. The covenants are all quite broad so there should be no reason a kindred can't find a place. As someone else said, there are two kinds; those who haven't chosen yet and the covenants should be trying to grab him or those that aren't going to join one and they are treated worse than the Carthians. The only unaligned I played with was a vampire staked and transported from Russia to the US before he knew what he became. The Unaligned should be a rare occurrence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:10:20-07:00","id":517020,"title":"","content":"Counterfeiting can be fixed. As for elders not needing blood - that's neglible. An elder provides a source of vitae to the bank, and he might exchange the money to buy vampire blood. This should probably be a Carthian thing, because they want to apply new governmental types... like capitalism.<br /> <br /> You could even have a Carthian Law protecting the money from counterfeiting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:11:26-07:00","id":517022,"title":"","content":"Thus the devotion/bloodline idea to address the counterfeiting. <br /> <br /> I really like the varying &quot;value&quot; of notes to cover different types, or different amounts of blood. This is a fun idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:44:05-07:00","id":517048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517020#post517020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should probably be a Carthian thing, because they want to apply new governmental types... like capitalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Capitalism is an economic system, not a governing system. I mean, I wouldn't put it past the Carthians to experiment with a society that's literally governed by its currency, but that's not how it's normally supposed to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:00:49-07:00","id":517051,"title":"","content":"Anarcho-Capitalist Libertarian Carthians are something I could totally see, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:26:47-07:00","id":517088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517051#post517051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarcho-Capitalist Libertarian Carthians are something I could totally see, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, without a doubt. Isn't that the Carthian dream? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:27:08-07:00","id":517089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517022#post517022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus the devotion/bloodline idea to address the counterfeiting.<br /> <br /> I really like the varying &quot;value&quot; of notes to cover different types, or different amounts of blood. This is a fun idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dislike it. Why have different notes for different stuff when you can have varrying amounts of notes? You know, like actual money is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:28:17-07:00","id":517090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517088#post517088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, without a doubt. Isn't that the Carthian dream? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So that means that Capitalism can be a form of government :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:29:18-07:00","id":517091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517089#post517089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I dislike it. Why have different notes for different stuff when you can have varrying amounts of notes? You know, like actual money is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I was thinking you'd have different denominations of currency. That's what I meant by different value. So a 1, 5, 10, 20 etc. which covers whatever combination. I worded it poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:49:33-07:00","id":517103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517090#post517090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that means that Capitalism can be a form of government :P</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the &quot;anarcho&quot; part of Anarcho-Capitalist Libertarian kind of precludes that possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:56:01-07:00","id":517107,"title":"","content":"Anarchy is a type of government... So, yes, it is. It's just that the type means that there's no centralised government and the subtypes of anarchy define more clearly by what rules the society is governing themselves. In Anarcho-Capitalist type of anarchy, it's money. In more traditional paths of anarchy the people govern themselves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To SwarmyVamp - missunderstandings happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:06:22-07:00","id":517110,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T17:08:19-07:00","id":517440,"title":"","content":"Anarchy is defined as an absence of government so... I think you mean democracy, as in its literal definition of &quot;mob rule.&quot; You have the majority making the decisions and the minority are fucked. Nobody in charge would define themselves as anarchists. It is a label put on others, like criminal. A democratic capitalist would be voting based on the amount of money a person has, that would be interesting. I've heard libertarians put forth similar ideas to that, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T18:51:29-07:00","id":517523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517440#post517440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchy is defined as an absence of government so... I think you mean democracy, as in its literal definition of &quot;mob rule.&quot; You have the majority making the decisions and the minority are fucked. Nobody in charge would define themselves as anarchists. It is a label put on others, like criminal. A democratic capitalist would be voting based on the amount of money a person has, that would be interesting. I've heard libertarians put forth similar ideas to that, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div> No government is a still a form of government, just as refusing to make a choice is, itself, a choice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T19:18:50-07:00","id":517546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517523#post517523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No government is a still a form of government, just as refusing to make a choice is, itself, a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cue Neil Peart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T02:13:25-07:00","id":517765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=517440#post517440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchy is defined as an absence of government so... I think you mean democracy, as in its literal definition of &quot;mob rule.&quot; You have the majority making the decisions and the minority are fucked. Nobody in charge would define themselves as anarchists. It is a label put on others, like criminal. A democratic capitalist would be voting based on the amount of money a person has, that would be interesting. I've heard libertarians put forth similar ideas to that, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I had some fancy response written, but then I scrolled up to reread everything before posting and I saw MCN's answer again and I think it hits the point directly with less mumbo jumbo I was about to post.. so.. What MCN said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:08:28-07:00","id":518488,"title":"","content":"I was not trying to be pedantic. I'm saying they would not call themselves anarchists if they are actually in charge. If they are in charge then they can't, by definition, be anarchists. I guess it is fine as a label for others to call them, but if we are talking about the authority in a domain then should we not focus more on how they identify themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:26:13-07:00","id":518510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=518488#post518488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not trying to be pedantic. I'm saying they would not call themselves anarchists if they are actually in charge. If they are in charge then they can't, by definition, be anarchists. I guess it is fine as a label for others to call them, but if we are talking about the authority in a domain then should we not focus more on how they identify themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchy kind of involves not having anyone &quot;in charge&quot;, so what you're saying here is a little tautological.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:26:48-07:00","id":518512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are in charge then they can't, by definition, be anarchists. </div> </div> </div>If you're in charge you can call youself whatever you want. History is full of regimes who fall short of the ideologies they promote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:31:09-07:00","id":518516,"title":"","content":"Anarchy disposes of a hierarchy and instead represents voluntary associations. There is no 'in charge' in an anarchy, otherwise you have a hierarchy. If you are the King of Mars you can call yourself an Anarchist but it doesn't make you one any more than calling yourself the King of Mars now makes you that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:41:56-07:00","id":518528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=518516#post518516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchy disposes of a hierarchy and instead represents voluntary associations. There is no 'in charge' in an anarchy, otherwise you have a hierarchy. If you are the King of Mars you can call yourself an Anarchist but it doesn't make you one any more than calling yourself the King of Mars now makes you that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They're just waiting until Kindred society is made ready for proper Anarchy. Plus there's the defence against the Invictus that needs managing, on a temporary basis of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:50:54-07:00","id":518530,"title":"","content":"I've lost track of why we're even talking about the definition of Anarchy at this point. I realize this derail was largely my fault, sorry for that, but can we try to bring this conversation back on topic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T16:26:47-07:00","id":518566,"title":"","content":"I tried by offering a suggestion to replace anarchy with something actually appropriate to describe a society that uses &quot;blood money&quot; which is certainly not an anarchy no matter what anyone wants to call them, including themselves, but everyone was more interested in arguing over semantics. Language is more than a little tautological, so if that was a complaint, what do you suggest? Am I supposed to draw pictures? Use allegory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T00:26:02-07:00","id":519042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/506095-the-unaligned?p=518566#post518566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried by offering a suggestion to replace anarchy with something actually appropriate to describe a society that uses &quot;blood money&quot; which is certainly not an anarchy no matter what anyone wants to call them, including themselves, but everyone was more interested in arguing over semantics. Language is more than a little tautological, so if that was a complaint, what do you suggest? Am I supposed to draw pictures? Use allegory?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A society solely run by &quot;blood money&quot; (ir just money) with no form of other government is Anarcho-Capitalism, a form of anarchy, so it's completely appropriate to use that for the topic. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anarcho-capitalism\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anarcho-capitalism</a> .<br /> <br /> As for the topic.. The Unaligned, uh? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}